<title>SOUTH AFRICA: HCI details rights offer terms.</title>
<headline>HCI details rights offer terms.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hosken Consolidated Investments Ltd (HCI) said on Tuesday it is to raise 186.3 million rand, before expenses, in a rights offer to fund its underwriting commitments in the Saflife Ltd offer.</p>
<p>Saflife is in the process of purchasing a 30 percent stake in JCI Ltd which sees the mining house transferred to black control.</p>
<p>HCI said it will be issuing around 43.84 million shares of 25 cents at an issue price of 425 cents each. Shareholders will be entitled to 19 new HCI shares for every 100 shares held.</p>
<p>It said the HCI rights offer has been fully underwritten for aan underwriting fee of 2.8 million rand, being 1.5 percent of the aggregated value of the subscription price of the new HCI shares.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
